# Digital Clock using Verilog

## Description
This project implements a digital clock using Verilog HDL.

The clock displays:
    HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS

The clock operates in 24-hour format.

Example:
    12:59:59
    13:00:00

## Inputs
- clk   : System clock
- reset : Active-high reset

## Outputs
- hours   : 5-bit hour counter (0-23)
- minutes : 6-bit minute counter (0-59)
- seconds : 6-bit second counter (0-59)

## Operation
The digital clock counts seconds as follows:

00:00:00
00:00:01
00:00:02
...
00:00:59
00:01:00
...
23:59:59
00:00:00

## Files

- digital_clock.v
    Main digital clock RTL design.

- tb_digital_clock.v
    Testbench for simulation.

- README.md
    Project documentation.

## Reset
When reset is HIGH, the clock is initialized to:

00:00:00

## Simulation
Compile using Icarus Verilog:

iverilog -o digital_clock_tb digital_clock.v tb_digital_clock.v

Run:

vvp digital_clock_tb

A VCD waveform file named digital_clock.vcd is also generated.
